ot diluting shareholders","ok":true,"evidence":"Diluted share count -6.2% YoY"},{"label":"Analyst estimates moving higher","ok":null,"evidence":"Estimate-revision feed not connected (Phase 2)"},{"label":"Management guidance increasing","ok":null,"evidence":"Earnings Intelligence Engine not built (Phase 2)"}],"thesis":"Adobe (ADBE) screens at opportunity 73.0 with an expectations gap of 26.0. Reality 59.0 reflects +12.0% TTM revenue growth, +35.7% operating margin and +59.4% ROIC; pricing 33.0 reflects a depressed multiple and neutral price momentum. Primary theme exposure: AI Software & Agents (trend 72.0). Macro fit for Technology in a Goldilocks regime is 53.0/100.","market_expectation":{"summary":"Priced for stagnation or deterioration; the market is not paying for improvement.","evidence":["EV/Sales 3.6x (0.0th pct of own 5y range)","P/E 13x (5.0th pct of own history)","FCF yield 11.4%","PEG 1.1","12m return -34%, -34% from 52w high"]},"what_market_misses":["Reality (59.0) is running ahead of what is priced (33.0): an expectations gap of +26 pts.","Its main theme (AI Software & Agents) has trend 72.0 vs pricing 53.0: the theme itself is under-owned."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (roughly 90 days after the last filing on 2026-09-22)","AI Software & Agents: evidence that 'Trust, integration into workflows, proprietary data' is easing via Platforms owning the system of record and the data","Continued rotation into Technology"],"risks":["No engine-flagged risks; standard execution and macro risk apply."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 7% (currently 12.0%)","ROIC falls below 45% (currently 59.4%)","Operating margin compresses more than 200 bps YoY (currently 35.7%)","Technology rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently +66)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55%","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength","AI Software & Agents theme trend drops below 45"],"break_rules":[{"id":"revenue_growth","label":"TTM revenue growth","metric":"revenue_growth","op":"<","threshold":0.0703,"current":0.1203},{"id":"roic","label":"ROIC","metric":"roic","op":"<","threshold":0.4452,"current":0.5935},{"id":"margin","label":"Operating margin change YoY","metric":"operating_margin_change","op":"<","threshold":-0.02,"current":-0.005463174840933449},{"id":"rotation","label":"Technology rotation score","metric":"sector_rotation","op":"<","threshold":-20,"consecutive":2,"current":66.0},{"id":"regime","label":"P(Stagflation)+P(Contraction)","metric":"adverse_regime_prob","op":">","threshold":55,"current":48.9},{"id":"trend","label":"Distance from 200dma","metric":"dist_200dma","op":"<","threshold":-10,"and_negative_rs":true,"current":-9.2},{"id":"theme","label":"AI Software & Agents theme trend","metric":"theme_trend","theme_id":"ai-software-agents","op":"<","threshold":45,"current":72.0}],"narrative_note":"Narrative from the last 7 morning briefs' theme signals (exposure-weighted).","llm_enriched":true,"theme_exposures":[{"theme_id":"ai-software-agents","theme":"AI Software & Agents","weight":0.4,"order":1,"effective":0.4}],"llm":{"thesis":"Adobe is being priced as a structurally impaired asset \u2014 12.8x earnings, 3.6x EV/Sales at the 0th percentile of its own five-year range, an 11.4% FCF yield and a 34% drawdown from the 52-week high \u2014 while the reported financials still show 12.0% TTM revenue growth (accelerating from 11.5%), 35.7% operating margins, 40.8% FCF margins and 59.4% ROIC. The gap between operating reality (59) and market pricing (33) is the trade: the market is underwriting generative-AI disintermediation of the creative suite, while the cash statements show no revenue deceleration yet. Management is monetizing the disbelief directly \u2014 $9.3bn of buybacks, a 6.2% reduction in diluted shares and a ~10% shareholder yield, which is why EPS grew 11.9% on only 4.7% net income growth. The risk is honest: the multiple can stay compressed for a long time if the market is right about terminal value rather than near-term numbers, and the tape (below the 200-day, MACD negative, RSI 38) says no one has re-rated it yet. This is a high-quality, cash-rich optionality position sized for a 2-4 quarter proof window rather than a momentum entry.","fundamental_read":"Growth is intact and mildly accelerating (+12.0% vs +11.5%), with best-in-class gross margin (89.3%), 40.8% FCF margin, 1.45x FCF conversion and 59.4% ROIC on an effectively unlevered balance sheet (net debt/EBITDA 0.07x, interest coverage 35.7x). The blemishes are real but small: operating margin fell 55bps YoY, SBC is 8.0% of revenue, and net income grew only 4.7% \u2014 well below the 11.9% EPS growth, meaning buybacks (not operating leverage) carried the per-share line. Incremental ROIC of 148.9% suggests the marginal dollar of revenue is still extremely profitable, which argues the margin dip is mix/investment, not structural price erosion \u2014 though one quarter cannot distinguish the two.","technical_read":"The trend is broken: price at 238.93 sits below the 20-, 50- and 200-day averages (262/257/263), 9.2% under the 200-day and 33.7% off the 52-week high, with MACD histogram at -3.47. The +23.5% three-month return followed by -12.8% over one month marks a failed rally back into the 50/200-day zone \u2014 a classic rejection, not a base. RSI 38 is weak but not washed out; a reclaim and hold above the ~257-263 moving-average cluster would be the first genuine trend-change evidence.","market_expectation":"At 5th-percentile P/E, 0th-percentile EV/Sales and an 11.4% FCF yield against a 28.6x historical median P/E, the market is discounting terminal-value impairment \u2014 that generative AI collapses the pricing power of creative tools, that seat growth stalls, and that today's 12% growth and 36% margins are a peak to be mean-reverted rather than a run-rate. Equivalently, the multiple implies near-zero long-term growth and margin decay; the market is paying for the cash flows it can see this year and nothing for the franchise beyond.","what_market_misses":["Reality score 59 vs pricing 33 \u2014 a 26-point expectations gap; revenue is accelerating, not decelerating, which is inconsistent with a disruption-in-progress narrative that should first show up in top-line deceleration and net revenue retention.","A ~10% shareholder yield funded entirely from internally generated cash with a 0.07x net-debt/EBITDA balance sheet: at this multiple, buybacks shrink the share count ~6%/yr, so even zero revenue growth produces mid-single-digit EPS growth. The market is treating the buyback as a value trap rather than as compounding optionality.","The primary theme exposure (AI Software & Agents) carries trend 72 vs theme pricing 53 \u2014 the theme is under-owned, and Adobe is being scored as an AI victim rather than an AI distributor despite owning the system of record and proprietary creative data.","Incremental ROIC of 148.9% implies the marginal revenue dollar is still hugely accretive; a -55bp margin print is more consistent with front-loaded AI infrastructure and go-to-market spend than with price competition.","Technology sector rotation is +66, the strongest of any sector, yet ADBE is -34% over 12 months \u2014 it is a rotation laggard inside a favored sector, which is where mean-reversion capital typically looks first."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (~90 days after the 2026-09-22 filing): the decisive datapoint is whether revenue growth holds above ~11% and whether operating margin stops compressing.","Disclosure of AI-attributable ARR or seat-level monetization that converts the AI narrative from cost to revenue.","Continued buyback execution at a 5th-percentile multiple \u2014 a further 5-6% share count reduction mechanically lifts EPS and lowers the implied multiple.","Technology sector rotation (+66) broadening from megacap AI infrastructure into under-owned application software.","Technical trigger: a weekly close back above the 257-263 moving-average cluster with positive relative strength would confirm that sellers are exhausted."],"risks":["The disruption thesis may be correct and simply early \u2014 generative AI eroding seat economics would show first in renewal pricing and net retention, neither of which is visible in the provided data.","Operating margin already fell 55bps YoY; if AI compute and model costs scale with usage, a 36% margin could structurally reset lower even with flat revenue.","Net income grew only 4.7% while EPS grew 11.9% \u2014 the quality of EPS growth is deteriorating; buyback-driven EPS is not a durable substitute for operating leverage.","SBC at 8.0% of revenue is a real economic cost partly masked by the buyback; true shareholder yield is lower than the headline 10%.","Regime probabilities are near-uniform (Goldilocks 26.6 / Contraction 25.4 / Stagflation 23.5) \u2014 macro fit for Technology is only 53/100, so there is no regime tailwind to lean on.","Price momentum is negative on every intermediate measure; cheap can get cheaper and a 0th-percentile EV/Sales has no historical support level to anchor to.","Coverage is only 0.75 \u2014 estimate revisions and management guidance feeds are not connected, so the single most important disconfirming signal (analysts cutting numbers) is unobserved."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth decelerates below ~9-10% in the next print, confirming the disruption narrative in the top line.","Operating margin compresses more than 200bps YoY, indicating AI cost-to-serve is structural rather than transitional.","ROIC falls below 45% or incremental ROIC turns sharply negative.","Buyback pace slows materially or share count stops shrinking \u2014 removing the primary EPS support at a depressed multiple.","Price fails to reclaim the 200-day (263) within two quarters and makes a new 52-week low on rising volume.","Technology sector rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs, removing the sector tailwind.","AI Software & Agents theme trend drops below 45, or evidence emerges that proprietary-data moats in creative workflows are being commoditized."],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Cloud and accelerated-compute providers: Adobe's generative features require inference at scale, and its capex is only $214m against $25.97bn of revenue \u2014 meaning the compute burden is being rented, not built, which transfers margin to hyperscalers and GPU suppliers.","Inference-optimization and model-serving software: the constraint that compressed Adobe's operating margin 55bps is cost-per-generation; whoever lowers that cost captures part of the recovered margin across the entire creative-software category.","Content provenance, rights management and licensed training-data marketplaces: Adobe's moat claim rests on commercially safe, proprietary data, which creates demand for attribution, watermarking and licensing infrastructure.","Enterprise data integration and identity/workflow middleware: if 'trust, integration into workflows, proprietary data' is the gating constraint for AI agents, the vendors that plumb systems of record to agents monetize regardless of which application layer wins.","Activist and value-oriented capital pools: a 12.8x P/E, 11.4% FCF yield, unlevered balance sheet and 10% shareholder yield is precisely the profile that attracts balance-sheet-activist pressure to lever up and accelerate repurchases."],"epistemic_labels":[{"statement":"TTM revenue grew 12.0% vs 11.5% in the prior quarter; operating margin 35.7% (-55bps YoY); ROIC 59.4%; FCF $10.59bn on $25.97bn revenue.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"P/E 12.8x at the 5th percentile of its own history (median 28.6x); EV/Sales 3.6x at the 0th percentile (median 7.6x); FCF yield 11.4%.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Diluted share count fell 6.2% YoY on $9.295bn of buybacks; net income grew 4.7% while EPS grew 11.9%.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Price 238.93 is below the 20/50/200-day averages, 9.2% under the 200-day, 33.7% off the 52-week high, RSI 38, MACD histogram -3.47.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"The market is discounting generative-AI disintermediation of Adobe's creative franchise and terminal-value impairment.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"The 55bp margin decline reflects front-loaded AI infrastructure and go-to-market investment rather than price competition, given 148.9% incremental ROIC.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"A ~6%/yr share count reduction means even zero revenue growth produces mid-single-digit EPS growth.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Consensus expects Technology to continue leading (sector rotation +66) and the macro regime to remain Goldilocks-tilted, though probabilities are near-uniform.","kind":"consensus_expectation"},{"statement":"A 12.8x P/E with an unlevered balance sheet and 10% shareholder yield could attract balance-sheet activism or accelerated levered repurchases.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"Adobe's proprietary creative data and system-of-record position convert it from AI victim to AI distributor over the next several quarters.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"Estimate revisions and management guidance feeds are not connected (coverage 0.75), so the most direct disconfirming evidence is currently unobserved.","kind":"observed_fact"}],"confidence":0.58}},"technical":{"score":0,"passes":0,"criteria":{"above_150_200":false,"150_above_200":false,"200_rising_1m":false,"50_above_150_200":false,"above_50":false,"25pct_above_52w_low":false,"within_25pct_of_52w_high":false,"rs_positive_6m":false},"ready":false,"stage":"basing_or_downtrend","close":238.93,"sma50":257.41,"sma150":246.41,"sma200":263.2,"sma150_prev4w":248.55,"sma150_declining":true,"pct_above_52w_low":23.5,"pct_from_52w_high":-33.7,"rs_6m":-19.7,"rsi14":38.3,"atr20":10.175,"atr_pct":4.26,"overbought":false},"fundamentals":{"latest":{"peri